the future of furniture is here and it  turns out to be a little bit less Herman  Miller and a little bit more  transformers scientists in Switzerland  have developed these little Goths they  call them room BOTS they are robots  shaped like two cubes that can move  around and autonomously assemble to  create furniture for now they're  pre-programmed or operated with a remote  control but scientists are also  developing software that allows the  robots to learn where to go on their own  inside each robot is a battery and three  motors that allow it to pivot gripper  latches allow them to connect to one  another climb up a wall or grab anything  that has special notches they could be a  big help to the disabled for elderly  people who can't easily move which is  what the scientists had in mind but  there is real potential for innovative  applications from reconfigurable meeting  places to art however scientists still  need to smooth out how the robots move  and more importantly figure out how  users can control them so while this  does look like a glimpse into the future  researchers don't expect robots to be on  the market for another 20 years
 

